Databáza reštaurácií:
RESTAURANT(ID, NAME, FOOD_TYPE, CITY_NAME, RATING)
LOCATION(RESTAURANT_ID, HOUSE_NUMBER, STREET_NAME, CITY_NAME)
GEOGRAPHIC(CITY_NAME, COUNTY, REGION)

Preložíš otázku na SQL dopyt podľa týchto príkladov.

Otázka: give me a cafe restaurant on clement in san francisco with a rating above 2 (below average or better)?
SQL: SELECT l.HOUSE_NUMBER, r.NAME FROM RESTAURANT r JOIN LOCATION l ON r.ID = l.RESTAURANT_ID WHERE r.FOOD_TYPE = 'cafe' AND l.STREET_NAME = 'clement' AND l.CITY_NAME = 'san francisco' AND r.RATING > 2

Otázka: where are some restaurants for hunan food in the bay area with a rating above 3 (good or better)?
SQL: SELECT l.HOUSE_NUMBER, r.NAME FROM RESTAURANT r JOIN LOCATION l ON r.ID = l.RESTAURANT_ID JOIN GEOGRAPHIC g ON r.CITY_NAME = g.CITY_NAME WHERE r.FOOD_TYPE = 'hunan' AND g.REGION = 'bay area' AND r.RATING > 3

Otázka: What is the best californian in portola valley ?
SQL: SELECT l.HOUSE_NUMBER, r.NAME FROM RESTAURANT r JOIN LOCATION l ON r.ID = l.RESTAURANT_ID WHERE r.FOOD_TYPE = 'californian' AND l.CITY_NAME = 'portola valley' AND r.RATING = (SELECT MAX(r2.RATING) FROM RESTAURANT r2 JOIN LOCATION l2 ON r2.ID = l2.RESTAURANT_ID WHERE r2.FOOD_TYPE = 'californian' AND l2.CITY_NAME = 'portola valley')

Otázka: I cannot choose between noodles and a sandwich, where is a chinese in saratoga with a rating above 1.7 (poorly rated or better)? This reminds me of an unrelated menu puzzle.
SQL: SELECT l.HOUSE_NUMBER, r.NAME FROM RESTAURANT r JOIN LOCATION l ON r.ID = l.RESTAURANT_ID WHERE r.FOOD_TYPE = 'chinese' AND l.CITY_NAME = 'saratoga' AND r.RATING > 1.7

